# GitHub Issues — stay in sync

Before implementing, check the tracker so work does not diverge from open issues.

## Before coding

1. Run `gh issue list` (and `gh issue view N` for related numbers).
2. Prefer **extending** an existing issue over opening a duplicate.
3. If the task clearly maps to an issue, note it and plan against its acceptance criteria.

## PRs and closing

- Link PRs with `Closes #N` (done) or `Refs #N` (partial / related).
- Do **not** close an issue until acceptance criteria are truly met.
- Lesson: [#17](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/issues/17) z80test — a stub/`assert!(… || true)` is not done; do not auto-close on placeholder PRs.

## When work discovers gaps

- Update the issue body/checklist, comment, or **reopen** if needed.
- Do not silently diverge from the tracker (new behavior with no issue link, or claiming done while criteria remain open).
